## Scenarios

### trait default strict shared bindings

#### derives the concrete default method type as a value

- Verify: derives the concrete default method type as a value
   - Expected: shell_write_text(fixture, trait_default_fixture()) is true
   - Expected: rc equals `0`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 11 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-COMPILER-BOOTSTRAP-001
step("Verify: derives the concrete default method type as a value")
val fixture = "build/land11_spec_fx/trait_default_binding.spl"
expect(shell_write_text(fixture, trait_default_fixture())).to_equal(true)
val (out, _err, rc) = rt_process_run_timeout(compiler_binary(), ["run", fixture], 300000)
expect(rc).to_equal(0)
# The DEFAULT method (greet, provided by the trait) and the IMPL
# method (who) must both resolve on the same concrete instance: the
# default method type was derived for Person, not kept as an
# unbound/optional value.
expect(out).to_contain("hello ada")
```

